ransformers these human  cybertronian symbionts are one form of  what's known as a headmaster with a  human literally transforming into the  bot's head other times like in the idw  continuation transformers regeneration 1  the humans gained superpowers allowing  them to battle the giant pods whether  our planet hosts energon the all-spark  powerful artifacts or just good  old-fashioned human interference it  seems humanity's home has fated to  intersect with the transformer's endless  war  unicron was is and will be again the  massive planet-eater first threatens the  transformers in the 1986 animated film  set in the far-flung future of 2006.  unicron reformats megatron into  galvatron and creates a new more deadly  breed of decepticon stepping up to fill  the shoes of a temporarily deceased  optimus prime hot rod becomes radimus  prime and defeats the galactic devourer  once and for all sort of after unicron  was defeated in the animated film he  made a detour through the marvel comics  continuity terrorizing their universe  instead his first appearance in the  series is notable for setting up  unicron's god-like powers and his  ability to manipulate the fabric of time  pulling galvatron out of the future  since then across these timelines and  multiverses unicron's return has become  all but inevitable in 2018 after over a  decade of avoiding the ultimate evil idw  comics finally brought unicronk back  with a vengeance the massive battle  unified the transformers and brought 13  years of comic book battle to an end  unicron also appears in the live-action  movies where transformers the last night  reveals that unicron is the earth itself  so it seems that we've not seen the last  of the planet eater after all  nearly every transformer story brings  the robots to earth as they flee  cybertron but there is one notable  exception 2001's transformers robots and  disguise cartoon is a bit of a wild card  robots in disguise does take place on  earth but instead of an ancient war  spilling over onto our planet this  particular show sees optimus prime  leading his autobots to prevent megatron  and his predacons from locating an  ancient cybertronian secret the  immensely powerful fortress maximus the  show never gets into these transformers  history much but there are some  interesting quirks to unpack this  version of ultra magnus for instance is  optimus prime's brother rather than an  old friend and on the topic of quirks  who could forget megatron's six-changer  form in this reality the predacon can  transform into among other things a  giant floating hand a bat and a  two-headed dragon as for the decepticons  the only ones in the entire universe are  created when megatron gets his hands on  a small handful of autobot protoforms  essentially blank slates and brainwashes  them into sinister new creations robots  in disguise was the first time a  japanese-produced transformer series was  adapted for western audiences born from  the car robots anime this adaptation was  also the first taste of what would  become countless official transformers  reboots before this point each new comic  or cartoon would simply tweak generation  1's continuity to fit its plot but  robots in disguise cut the timeline  loose and gave creators free reign as a  result transformers lore has since run  wildly in every imaginable direction  [Laughter]  i found my very own minicon and megatron  will love me for this launched in 2004  transformers armada was the second full  reboot to the transformers timeline in  the world of armada there aren't just  autobots and decepticons there's also a  third faction called minicons in this  timeline unicron disguises himself as a  cybertronian moon and creates some mini  cons to kick the autobot and decepticon  war into high gear the tiny bots have  the ability to boost the power of their  larger brethren naturally leading to the  autobots and decepticons struggling for  control over this new breed of  transformers eventually both factions  realize the mini cons are too dangerous  and cast them off into the far reaches  of space predictably the minicons end up  on earth where they are rediscovered  millions of years later by the  cybertronians this brings the  transformers into the modern era and as  is tradition drags humans into their  fight unicron is defeated by the end of  armada but his story continues in two  more series transformers enter jon jumps  into the then near future of 2010 and  chronicles yet another resurrection of  the planet eater transformers cybertron  sees the transformers fleeing to earth  after the black hole left by unicron's  destruction threatens their home planet  though it's one of the pillars of the  transformers multiverse this alternate  timeline had quite a few detractors and  the repeated focus on unicron left  audiences more than a little burnt out  though 2007's live action transformers  initially seemed to be a faithful homage  to generation 1 it would quickly grow  into an entirely new beast the  transformers in michael bay's films are  not creations of primus but of a  mysterious alien race not so cleverly  dubbed the creators the later films  retconned a lot about the earlier ones  but the important parts is that the  transformers come to earth about 19 000  years before modern times at this point  the cybertronians plan to harvest our  sun for energon until they discover  humans and mostly agree not to wipe us  out but the fallen one of the original  transformers from the dynasty of primes  wants to take the sun anyways this  sparks the division of the transformers  and the formation of the decepticons in  other words this is a rare timeline  where the great war isn't sparked by  megatron but his master the fallen is  eventually defeated but the war rages on  a recurring habit to the bay films is to  interweave cybertronian history into our  own in the 2007 film they're revealed to  have been responsible for humanity's  technological advancement in dark of the  moon they're the reason for the space  race in age of extinction the creators  were responsible for eradicating the  dinosaurs and according to the last  knight they aided king arthur and fought  alongside the allied forces in both  world wars the transformers had been on  earth for centuries by the events of the  first film but the autobot decepticon  war flares up once again when the  all-spark was rediscovered kicking off  the entire live-action series  it's you and me megatron no it's just me  prime  then 2018's bumblebee once again changed  the live-action universe and rebooted  the entire story instead of transformers  landing on earth millions of years ago  bumblebee becomes the first autobot to  land on earth in 1987. he encounters a  couple of decepticons who also landed on  earth as he awaits the arrival of  optimus prime and other autobots as they  flee the war happening on cybertron  while much of transformers passed is  relegated to hazy constantly changing  myths the future remains a diverging  branch of possibilities in 2008's  transformers animated the autobots win  the great war by shooting the all-spark  into space and keeping its power out of  megatron's hands ultra magnus then leads  the autobots to victory after which  cybertron thrives while megatron and the  decepticons flee to the fringes as  renegades this iteration of optimus  prime is just a young asteroid miner who  stumbles upon the allspark years later  in modern times the inevitable clash  between his crew and megatron sends them  crashing to earth where they lie dormant  for just 50 years when they awaken a  22nd century earth they find the planet  awash in robots thanks to a human  scientist who reverse engineered  megatron's body and created his own  mechanical life animated is one of the  more unique takes on transformers  history two beast wars characters even  make an appearance black arachnia and  waspinator if it weren't so wildly  detached from established series lore  this next generation continuity could  have been an interesting bridge between  the robotic transformers of past and  present in the tech organic bots of the  future  in a franchise as diverging and messy as  transformers it's hard to say which  ending is the definitive finale but one  particular series provides a better  candidate than others the beast wars  sequel series beast machines  the predacon leader enslaves all of  cybertron reformatting maximals and  predacons alike into mindless drone  servants the beast machines cartoon is a  dark dystopian tale where a handful of  maximals led by optimus primal fight a  guerrilla battle in a war that was over  before it started the story introduces a  number of fascinating concepts  transformers are more like cyborgs and  beast machines as they embrace their  organic sides and become techno-organic  creatures ones that don't so much  transform rather morphing between their  alternate forms what are we robots or  animals  both  and neither well that sure clears it up  this future even has botanica what is  believed to be the only plant-based  transformer in all the multiversal  timeline the series ends with maximals  freeing cybertron for megatron's control  thereby saving the planet the entire  transformer race is reborn into foley  tech organic beans ushering in a new  golden age of cybertron outside of the  beast machines cartoon this future was  only ever briefly explored in a couple  of short-lived comic books so while this  techno-organic cybertronian destiny  isn't quite a universal ending it  provides the closest thing to a final  happy ending the transformers franchise  has ever received  [Music]
 

